One further check is a warning rather than an error. Under \code{model = "v4"}
with a free \code{sigma}, a flat intercept is admissible only if \code{a > 1}, and the
historical default \code{a = 1} sits exactly on the divergent boundary. That
configuration is what Experiments v4 and v6 ran, so it stays available and
warns instead of failing.
